    "description": "Các buổi kiểm tra/ôn tập theo FLM.",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">RMD301 · Assessments</span>\n<h2>When you are tested</h2></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">RMD301 · Kiểm tra & thi</span>\n<h2>Khi nào bị kiểm tra</h2></div>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Topic<br><small>Nội dung</small></th><th>LO</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>DESIGN AS PRACTICE, RESEARCH AND THINKING<br>- Design Practice<br>- Design research<br>- Design Thinking</td><td>CLO1</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>RESEARCH ESSENTIALS<br>- Defining a research problem<br>- Formulating a research statement<br>- Framing a research question or a hypothesis<br>- Review of the literature<br>- Glossary of key terms</td><td>CLO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>RESEARCH ESSENTIALS (Continued)<br>- Understanding research methods and methodologies<br>- Choosing a research approach<br>- Research triangulation<br>- Multimethod research<br>- Ethical research</td><td>CLO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>RESEARCH ESSENTIALS (Continued)<br>- Writing a research proposal</td><td>CLO2</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>ETHNOGRAPHIC RESEARCH<br>- What is ethnography?<br>- Conducting ethnography research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>8</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>ETHNOGRAPHIC RESEARCH (Continued)<br>- Data collecting<br>- Ethics and research participants<br>- Data analysis</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>9</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>ETHNOGRAPHIC RESEARCH (Continued)<br>- Preparing a report<br>- Hallmarks of good ethnographic research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>10</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>QUALITATIVE RESEARCH<br>- What is qualitative research<br>- Case studies</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>11</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>QUALITATIVE RESEARCH (Continued)<br>- Phenomenology<br>- Historical research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>12</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>QUALITATIVE RESEARCH (Continued)<br>- Grounded theory<br>- Hallmarks of good qualitative research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>13</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>QUANTITATIVE RESEARCH<br>- What is qualitative research<br>- Survey</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>14</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>QUANTITATIVE RESEARCH (Continued)</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>15</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>QUANTITATIVE RESEARCH (Continued)<br>- Hallmarks of good quantitative research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>16</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>VISUAL RESEARCH<br>- What is visual research?<br>- Visual and material culture studies<br>- Hallmark of good visual research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>17</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>APPLIED RESEARCH<br>- What is applied research?<br>- Action research<br>- Hallmark of good applied research</td><td>CLO3</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>18</strong></td><td>PRESENTATION<br>PRESENTING YOUR RESEARCH<br>- Research report<br>- Executive summary<br>- Design brief<br>- Design report</td><td>CLO4, CLO5</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>"
